domain VT104_STORAGE:
  description "Prepare owner-managed snapshot storage candidate before real capture."
evidence OWNER_REQUEST:
  "Owner explicitly requested creation of a storage destination candidate, not resource creation or capture."
evidence GCP_READBACK:
  "2026-09-30 project kshiai bucket list returns one bucket kshiai_cloudbuild in US, uniform bucket access false, public access prevention inherited. Active authenticated account mako10k@mk10.org. Current list is bounded to this project and account."
evidence PLATFORM:
  "Official Cloud Storage documentation supports Google-managed default encryption, uniform bucket IAM, enforced public access prevention, retention policy and lifecycle deletion. Retention/lifecycle/soft-delete interact, and project IAM privileges remain inherited."
premise PROTECTION:
  "Snapshot includes private application state and requires protected beneficiary owner, precise storage/access/encryption/retention/readback and measured restore bound before shared stopped cutover. Owner-only access cannot be claimed until inherited IAM and recovery executor are verified."
premise OPTION_SHARED:
  "Reuse existing US Cloud Build bucket."
premise OPTION_DEDICATED:
  "Propose dedicated asia-northeast1 Standard bucket with public prevention enforced, uniform bucket access, default Google-managed encryption/TLS, owner-admin and frozen executor minimal object-create/read roles,30-day unlocked retention and lifecycle deletion with7-day soft delete explicitly included."
premise OPTION_OFFLINE:
  "Owner local encrypted archive avoids new cloud storage but adds export/device/key/transfer dependencies and unmeasured restore duration."
pending EXECUTOR:
  "Exact service account, inherited privileged principals, globally available bucket name, archive coverage/dependencies and real transfer/restore/forward recovery timings need independent verification."
decision SELECT based_on OWNER_REQUEST, GCP_READBACK, PLATFORM, PROTECTION, OPTION_SHARED, OPTION_DEDICATED, OPTION_OFFLINE, EXECUTOR:
  "Recommend dedicated bucket candidate for review. Existing build bucket is poorly matched to separate private snapshot policy. Preserve30day minimum plus7day recoverable soft-delete as retention proposal, not exact deletion deadline. Prepare configuration and max-write/readback fields; resource creation/export remain separate execution packet authority."

evidence INHERITED_IAM:
  "Project IAM readback shows owner mako10k@mk10.org and default compute service account with project editor plus storage.objectViewer. A new bucket in this project inherits these privileges; bucket-only IAM does not make plaintext owner-only."
evidence AGE_PRIMARY:
  "Official age documentation supports recipient public-key encryption and private identity decryption. The local age executable is currently unavailable; no owner key or encryption run exists."
premise OPTION_ENCRYPTED:
  "Add owner-recipient client-side age encryption before dedicated bucket upload. Inherited privileged project principals can access ciphertext; plaintext requires owner-controlled private identity. Key loss blocks recovery, so a protected backup and owner-assisted actual restore rehearsal are prerequisites."
decision REVISED_STORAGE based_on SELECT, INHERITED_IAM, AGE_PRIMARY, OPTION_ENCRYPTED, OWNER_REQUEST:
  "Recommend dedicated bucket with client-side owner-recipient encryption,30day minimum retention and7day soft-delete proposal. Preserve exact inherited-reader disclosure. Collect owner public recipient and protected key recovery route before execution. Keep plaintext owner-only as a verification condition, not an already achieved state."

evidence OWNER_SELECTION:
  "Owner explicitly selected option1 owner public-key pre-encryption with disclosed common dedicated Tokyo GCS30day minimum and7day soft-delete. Selection is storage policy only, not resource creation or actual capture/production action. Public recipient/private identity storage remain pending."
premise LOCAL_TOOL_CHECK:
  "Prepare an isolated official Ubuntu age binary without system installation, verify package and repository metadata, and run synthetic key/encrypt/decrypt/wrong-key/tamper tests. Fixture keys are temporary test doubles, not owner keys. No private production state or remote upload."
decision RECORD_AND_VERIFY based_on OWNER_SELECTION, LOCAL_TOOL_CHECK, PROTECTION:
  "Record Accepted storage policy ADR and subordinate packet fields. Test the encryption tool locally with synthetic data and preserve exact version/hash evidence. Prepare owner-key procedure as needed, without creating an owner key at an unspecified protection destination."
